ow who processes it or how: it only publishes"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"h","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":90.0,"h":30.0,"text":"handler","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e0","x1":116.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":160.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":50.0,"h":30.0,"text":"bcast","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":206.0,"y1":62.0,"x2":256.0,"y2":40.0,"tone":"muted","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":206.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":256.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"muted","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e3","x1":206.0,"y1":78.0,"x2":256.0,"y2":100.0,"tone":"muted","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":300.0,"y":40.0,"w":70.0,"h":22.0,"text":"client 1","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":300.0,"y":70.0,"w":70.0,"h":22.0,"text":"client 2","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":300.0,"y":100.0,"w":70.0,"h":22.0,"text":"client 3","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"h","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":90.0,"h":30.0,"text":"handler","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e0","x1":116.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":170.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"q","x":200.0,"y":70.0,"w":70.0,"h":30.0,"text":"queue","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":236.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":276.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"w","x":320.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":30.0,"text":"background\ntask","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":10.0,"y":20.0,"lines":["state.events.send(Event::Message(msg));","// who is subscribed is not our concern"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":30.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.0,23.9]}]},{"title":"FromRef","sub":"Sub-states","short":"FromRef","main":"FromRef lets a handler ask for part of the state: only the config or only the pool.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Narrow window","FromRef","Easier tests"],"captions":["The handler needs the config, not the whole application","FromRef extracts a clone of the needed field from the state","A test supplies only the needed part"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":130.0,"h":70.0,"text":"AppState\nconfig\npool\nhub","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":156.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":218.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"muted","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":290.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"State<Config>","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":20.0,"lines":["impl FromRef<AppState> for Config {","    fn from_ref(s: &AppState) -> Config {","        s.config.clone()","    }","}"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":26.0,"text":"handler(State<Config>)","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":90.0,"y":110.0,"w":130.0,"h":26.0,"text":"test: Config::test()","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":160.0,"y1":98.0,"x2":160.0,"y2":74.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":290.0,"y":85.0,"text":"no pool\nand no hub","tone":"muted","size":9.0}]],"cues":[12.6,25.2]}]},{"title":"State and Extension","sub":"Static and dynamic","short":"Extension","main":"State is known at build time, Extension is added on the fly, for example by an auth layer.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["State","Extension","What goes where"],"captions":["Known when the router is built; checked by the compiler","Put into the request on the fly; taken by the Extension<T> extractor","Permanent things go in State, request data in Extension"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":130.0,"h":30.0,"text":"with_state(app)","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":156.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":214.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":290.0,"y":70.0,"w":130.0,"h":30.0,"text":"checked at build time","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"auth layer","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":120.0,"y1":40.0,"x2":164.0,"y2":40.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":210.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"req.extensions","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":260.0,"y1":54.0,"x2":260.0,"y2":96.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":260.0,"y":110.0,"w":130.0,"h":26.0,"text":"Extension<UserId>","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":80.0,"y":110.0,"text":"no layer → 500","tone":"red","size":9.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":50.0,"w":130.0,"h":26.0,"text":"pool, config, hub","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":50.0,"w":110.0,"h":26.0,"text":"State","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":156.0,"y1":50.0,"x2":214.0,"y2":50.0,"tone":"muted","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":90.0,"y":110.0,"w":130.0,"h":26.0,"text":"who came, request ID","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":270.0,"y":110.0,"w":110.0,"h":26.0,"text":"Extension","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":156.0,"y1":110.0,"x2":214.0,"y2":110.0,"tone":"muted","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[12.9,25.8]}]},{"title":"tower layers","sub":"Layer and Service","short":"Layers","main":"A Layer wraps a Service in another Service: logic before and after the inner service call.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Layer","Matryoshka","ServiceBuilder"],"captions":["A Layer takes a service and returns a new one, with logic around the call","The outer one sees the request first and gets the response last","ServiceBuilder lists layers top to bottom, in execution order"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":20.0,"lines":["trait Layer<S> {","    type Service;","    fn layer(&self, inner: S) -> Self::Service;","}"],"hl":[2],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":85.0,"w":170.0,"h":130.0,"text":"","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":85.0,"w":120.0,"h":90.0,"text":"","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":180.0,"y":85.0,"w":70.0,"h":40.0,"text":"handler","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":30.0,"text":"layer 1","tone":"muted","size":9.0},{"t":"text","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":52.0,"text":"layer 2","tone":"muted","size":9.0},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":60.0,"y1":85.0,"x2":120.0,"y2":85.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":20.0,"lines":["ServiceBuilder::new()","    .layer(TraceLayer::new_for_http())   // outside","    .layer(TimeoutLayer::new(secs))      // inside","    .service(handler)"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"rust","size":8.5,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[11.8,23.6]}]},{"title":"from_fn","sub":"Custom middleware","short":"from_fn","main":"middleware::from_fn turns async fn(req, next) into a layer with no manual Service implementation.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Layer function","Before and after","With state"],"captions":["async fn(req, next) -> Response instead of a manual Service implementation","Before next we change the request or reply ourselves, after it we change the response","from_fn_with_state gives access to the shared state"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":20.0,"lines":["async fn mw(req: Request, next: Next) -> Response {","    let res = next.run(req).await;","    res","}","app.layer(middleware::from_fn(mw))"],"hl":[0,4],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":14.0,"lines":["async fn auth(req: Request, next: Next) -> Response {","    if req.headers().get(AUTHORIZATION).is_none() {","        return StatusCode::UNAUTHORIZED.into_response();","    }","    let mut res = next.run(req).await;","    res.headers_mut().insert(\"x-done\", \"1\".parse().unwrap());","    res","}"],"hl":[1,2,5],"lang":"rust","size":8.0,"lh":16.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":20.0,"lines":["app.layer(middleware::from_fn_with_state(","    state.clone(), count));","","async fn count(State(s): State<App>,","               req: Request, next: Next) -> Response"],"hl":[0,1,3],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.4,24.9]}]},{"title":"Layer order","sub":"Who is outside","short":"Order","main":"layer wraps everything added before it; route_layer only the routes; order decides.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["layer: the last is outermost","route_layer","ServiceBuilder: reversed"],"captions":["Router::layer wraps everything added before it: the last one sees the request first","route_layer does not affect requests to nonexistent paths: they bypass the layer","In ServiceBuilder the layer listed first is the outermost"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":20.0,"lines":["Router::new()","    .route(\"/x\", get(h))","    .layer(A)      // inside","    .layer(B)      // outside: B → A → h"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":80.0,"y":40.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"GET /x  → layer → h","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":80.0,"y":90.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"GET /zzz → 404","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":270.0,"y":40.0,"text":"with route_layer —\nwith the layer","tone":"muted","size":9.0},{"t":"text","id":"m","x":270.0,"y":90.0,"text":"layer — with the layer,\nroute_layer — without","tone":"muted","size":9.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":20.0,"lines":["ServiceBuilder::new()","    .layer(A)      // outside: A → B → h","    .layer(B)","    .service(h)"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"rust","s